    {
      "id": "u4989yx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Radius and General Facts about the Earth"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth consists of three principal concentric layers: Crust, Mantle, and Core.",
        "The Crust is subdivided into Continental Crust (Sial: Silica and Aluminium) and Oceanic Crust (Sima: Silica and Magnesium).",
        "The Mantle reaches a depth of 2,900 km and includes the semi-fluid Asthenosphere responsible for tectonic plate motion.",
        "The Core is divided into a liquid Outer Core (generating Earth's magnetic field) and a solid Inner Core.",
        "Internal boundaries are defined by seismic discontinuities including Conrad, Mohorovičić (Moho), Repetti, Gutenberg, and Lehmann."
      ],
      "id": "8l4iu12"
    },
