      "content": "Types of Core"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Moho Discontinuity lies between the Crust and Mantle, while Gutenberg Discontinuity separates the Mantle from the Core (~2,900 km depth).",
        "Sial forms the lighter continental crust, whereas Sima forms the denser oceanic crust.",
        "The Outer Core remains in a liquid state while the Inner Core is solid due to extreme pressure.",
        "Seismic S-waves cannot travel through the liquid outer core, producing an S-wave shadow zone beyond 103°."
      ],
      "id": "242hx8t"
    },
